# WordPress & WooCommerce Coding Standards

Refer to [wordpress-development-guidelines.md](mdc:.clinerules/wordpress-development-guidelines.md) for complete details. Essential points:

• Use strict typing where possible: `declare(strict_types=1);`
• Follow WordPress coding standards: camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for classes.
• Prefer hooks (`add_action`, `add_filter`) over editing core files.
• Sanitize and escape ALL inputs/outputs (`sanitize_text_field`, `esc_html`, etc.).
• Use `$wpdb->prepare()` for database queries; avoid raw SQL.
• Protect forms with nonces (`wp_verify_nonce`).
• Enqueue assets via `wp_enqueue_script()` / `wp_enqueue_style()`.
• Check WooCommerce activation & version before hooking.